|| 6.16.24 ||

 dehendriyaprāṇamanodhiyo'mī

yadaṃśaviddhāḥ pracaranti karmasu |

 naivānyadā lauham ivāprataptaṃ

 sthāneṣu tad draṣṭrapadeśam eti ||

śrīdharaḥ :  teṣāṃ tadajñāne hetum āha—dehendriyādayo'mī yadaṃśaviddhā
yaccaitanyāṃśenāviṣṭāḥ santaḥ karmasu svasvaviṣayeṣu pracaranti
jāgratsvapnayoḥ | anyadā suṣuptimūrcchādau naiva pracaranti, yathā
aprataptaṃ lohaṃ na dahati | ato yathā loham agniśaktyaiva dāhakaṃ sad
agniṃ vinā na dahati, evaṃ brahmagatajñānakriyāśaktibhyāṃ pravartamānā
dehādayas tan na spṛśanti na viduś ceti bhāvaḥ |

jīvas tarhi draṣṭṛtvāj jānātu ? nety āha—sthāneṣu jāgradādiṣu
draṣṭrapadeśaṃ draṣṭṛsaṃjñāṃ tad evaiti prāpnoti, nānyo jīvo nāmāsti,
nānyo'to'sti draṣṭā [bṛ.ā.u. 3.7.23] ityādiśruteḥ | yad vā,
draṣṭrapadeśaṃ draṣṭṛsaṃjñaṃ jīvam api tad evaiti jānāti, na tu jīvas
taj jānātīty arthaḥ | tad uktaṃ haṃsaguhyastotre deho'savo'kṣā [bhā.pu.
6.4.25] ityādi |

kramasandarbhaḥ :  dehendriya iti | atrādvaitaśārīrake'pi sāṅkhyam
ākṣipyoktaṃ, yathā, atha punaḥ sākṣinimittam īkṣitṛtvaṃ pradhānasya
kalpyeta yathāgninimittam ayaḥpiṇḍāder dagdhṛtvaṃ, tathā sati yan
nimittam īkṣitatṛtvaṃ pradhānasya, tad eva sarvajñaṃ mukhyaṃ jagataḥ
kāraṇam  [śaṅkarabhāṣya, 1.1.5] iti |

śrutiś cātra—tam eva bhāntam anubhāti [kaṭha.u. 2.2.15], ko hy evānyāt kaḥ
