|| 6.16.51 ||

 ahaṃ vai sarvabhūtāni bhūtātmā bhūtabhāvanaḥ |

śabdabrahma paraṃ brahma mamobhe śāśvatī tanū ||

madhvaḥ : haris tu sarvabhūtāni tadantaryāmyapekṣayā |

tiṅpadāny api sarvāṇi suppadāni tathaiva ca |

tasminn eva pravarteta mukhyā vṛttyā viśeṣataḥ || iti ca ||51||

śrīdharaḥ :  tad bodhadārḍhyāya svayam apy upadiśati, aham ityādinā |
sarvabhūtāny aham eva bhūtānām ātmā bhoktāpy aham eva |
bhoktṛbhogyātmakaṃ viśvaṃ madvyatiriktaṃ nāstīty arthaḥ | yato'haṃ
bhūtabhāvanaḥ bhūtānāṃ prakāśakaḥ kāraṇaṃ ca |

nanu śabdabrahma prakāśakaṃ, paraṃ brahma kāraṇaṃ ca prakāśakaṃ ca ?
satyam, te ubhe mamaiva rūpe ity āha—śabdabrahmeti | śāśvatī śāśvatyau
||51||

kramasandarbhaḥ :  aham iti | atra śabdabrahmaṇaḥ sāhacaryāt
parabrahmaṇo'py aṃśatvam āyāti ||51||

viśvanāthaḥ : kiṃ ca, bhaktitattvaṃ tvayā jñātam eva, tatra ajita jitaḥ
[bhā.pu. 6.16.35]  ityādistutir eva pramāṇam | jijñāsānairapekṣyārthaṃ
jñānatattvam aham evopadiśāmi, śṛṇv ity āha—ahaṃ vai iti | atredaṃ
vivecanīyam | vastu tāvat dvividhaṃ—vāstavam avāstavaṃ ca | brahma
paramātmā bhagavān saparikara ity etat tritayam eva vāstavaṃ vastu,
māyikaprapañcajātam idam avāstavaṃ vastu | avastu ca dvividhaṃ—kāryam
akāryaṃ ca | kāryaṃ svapnendrajālādigatam | akāryaṃ khapuṣpaśaśaśṛṅgādi
| eṣāṃ madhye, vedyaṃ vāstavam atra vastu  [bhā.pu. 1.1.2] iti
prathamokter vāstavavastuna evopādeyatvaṃ vaktuṃ, prathamam avāstavaṃ
vastv āha—sarvabhūtāni bhoktṛbhogyātmakāni jaganti aham eva,
madīyajīvaśaktimāyāśaktimayatvād iti bhāvaḥ | atra jīvānām
avāstavavastutvam avidyāvṛtatvād evoktam |

vāstavaṃ vastv āha—bhūtānāṃ samaṣṭivyaṣṭīnām ātmā antaryāmīti dvitīyaḥ |
tṛtīyaś ca puruṣo'ham | tathā bhūtāni tāni bhāvayatīty utpādayatīti
prathamaḥ puruṣaś cāham | tathā bhūtāni dāsyasakhyādibhāvavanti karotīti
bhūtabhāvanaḥ, kṛṣṇo rāmaś ca samprati tvayā dṛśyaś cāham |

kiṃ ca, niśvāsarūpaṃ yat śabdabrahma vedaḥ, tathā mannirviśeṣākāratvena
jñāniṣu pratipadyamānaṃ yat paraṃ brahma, te ubhe mamaiva tanurūpe |
vedasya śabdarūpatvād ākāśaguṇatvenānityaśaṅkāyās tathā parabrahmaṇaś
cānirdeśyatvenāvastutvaśaṅkāyā vāraṇāyāha—śāśvatī śāśvatyau nityasatye
eva ||51||

